.TH PKCSSLOTD 8 "August 2026" "@PACKAGE_VERSION@" "openCryptoki"
.SH NAME
pkcsslotd - shared memory manager for openCryptoki

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pkcsslotd

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBpkcsslotd\fP daemon coordinates PKCS#11-enabled applications that use
openCryptoki. It maintains a shared memory segment that tracks, per slot,
the number of open sessions across all processes, and reclaims sessions of
processes that terminate without calling \fBC_Finalize\fP.
.PP
\fBpkcsslotd\fP also delivers asynchronous events to running openCryptoki
applications over a Unix domain socket. This includes notifications about
cryptographic adapters (APQNs) becoming available or unavailable, and
coordination events used by the \fBpkcshsm_mk_change\fP(1) tool when
changing a hardware security module's master key.
.PP
At startup, \fBpkcsslotd\fP reads the \fBopencryptoki.conf\fP(5)
configuration file to determine which slots and tokens are available. It
passes this slot and token configuration to openCryptoki applications over
the same Unix domain socket during their \fBC_Initialize\fP call.

.SH NOTES
Only one instance of the pkcsslotd daemon should be running on any
given host. If a prior instance of pkcsslotd did not shut down
cleanly, then it may leave an allocated shared memory segment on
the system. The allocated memory segment can be identified by its
key and can be safely removed once the daemon is stopped with the
ipcrm command, such as:

\fIipcrm -M 0x6202AB38\fP

The daemon creates the shared memory segment with group ownership by the
\fI@pkcs_group@\fP group. All non-root users that should be able to use
openCryptoki need to be members of the group. Only trusted users should be
assigned to the group, see the "SECURITY NOTE" in the \fBopencryptoki\fP(7)
manual page for details.

\fBpkcsslotd\fP normally runs under the \fI@pkcsslotd_user@\fP user (and the
\fI@pkcs_group@\fP group). If started as \fBroot\fP, it performs its
privileged initialization steps and then drops privileges to the
\fI@pkcsslotd_user@\fP user before proceeding.

.SH "SEE ALSO"
.PD 0
.TP
\fBopencryptoki\fP(7),
.TP
\fBopencryptoki.conf\fP(5),
.TP
\fBpkcsconf\fP(1),
.TP
\fBpkcsstats\fP(1),
.TP
\fBpkcshsm_mk_change\fP(1).
.PD
